From 7414c0a7d3e600ca5db92ebdce56af1a22315e30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kirn Gill II <segin2005@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 15:57:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 15/98] =?UTF-8?q?fonts:=20port=20B&H=20Lucida=20+=20instal?=
 =?UTF-8?q?l=20CDE=20-dt-*=20aliases=20=E2=80=94=20fixes=20dtcm=20freezing?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20the=20desktop?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Opening dtcm froze the whole UI: the mouse cursor still moved but clicks
and keystrokes were dead.  Root cause (found via gdb + the Xfbdev log):

dtcm builds Motif FontSets from -b&h-lucida* and the CDE logical -dt-*
font names.  Neither was installed — there was no font-bh port (only
adobe + misc), and the CDE programs/fontaliases/{mixed,fixed}.alias were
never staged.  The FontSet build fails, and drawing text with the broken
set makes Xfbdev (the X server) SEGFAULT.  The server dies *holding the
evdev keyboard+mouse grab*, the ungrab fails (error 9), so the input
devices stay grabbed — cursor moves (hardware) but nothing receives
events.  That is the "stuck, mouse moves, clicks/keys do nothing" freeze.

Fix:
- contrib/font-bh-lucida/: new port for the X.Org B&H Lucida /
  LucidaTypewriter bitmap fonts (75 + 100 dpi), deriving ISO8859-1
  variants like font-adobe.
- build-rootfs.sh finalize_x_fonts(): after the contrib overlays,
  regenerate ONE merged fonts.dir per X font dir (adobe + bh share
  100dpi/75dpi) and install the CDE {mixed,fixed}.alias as fonts.alias so
  -dt-* resolves to the adobe fonts.

Verified headless: dtcm now starts and stays up, the "Cannot convert ...
to type FontSet" errors are gone, and Xfbdev no longer crashes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
